1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,990
Oh Ben. I just remembered I never filled in that form for Nick-did you do it?

2
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:10,390
The course feedback form?

3
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:14,660
Yes. If you want, we can do it together, I've got mine here.

4
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:15,500
Is that OK?

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Yeah.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,560
OK, let's have a look then. What do we have to do?

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:26,670
Let's fill in the top first, let's see, Course, Course code...

8
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:29,410
Er, it's Communication in Business.

9
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:36,930
OK, Communication... in... Business, I do know that, but what's the code?

10
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:41,120
CBI6 something, CB162, isn't it?

11
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,982
Mmm, that's it, OK and dates, when did we start?

12
00:00:44,982 --> 00:00:50,780
I remember, my birthday's on May 4th and it was the day after

13
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:52,320
it must have been May 5th.

14
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:54,390
Gosh, doesn't seem that long ago, does it?

15
00:00:54,390 --> 00:01:00,680
No, and we finish at the end of this week, on Friday, so that's July 15th?

16
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:05,309
Er 16th, Monday was the 12th. Right, that was the easy bit,

17
00:01:05,309 --> 00:01:06,880
now let's have a look

18
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:11,481
Please give your comments on the following aspects of the course",

19
00:01:11,481 --> 00:01:16,110
OK, what's the first one? Oh, course organisation. What do you think?

20
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:19,450
Er, clear? It was, wasn't it?

21
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:25,110
Yes, I think the organisation was clear. OK, anything else for course organisation?

22
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:29,510
It was a good thing he gave us the course outline at the beginning,

23
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:33,910
in the first session, that was useful, so I'll put that down, shall I?

24
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:38,193
Now, going on to suggestions for improvement, one thing that wasn't so good,

25
00:01:38,193 --> 00:01:42,900
I think we could have done a bit more work at the beginning

26
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,440
I mean at the beginning it seemed dead easy.

27
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,050
Yeah.

28
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:48,438
I thought it was going to be really easy

29
00:01:48,438 --> 00:01:53,743
and then all of a sudden in the second half of the course we got a whole load of work,

30
00:01:53,743 --> 00:01:55,600
reading to do and essays and things.

31
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,760
Yes, it'd be better if it was more even

32
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:02,070
OK, now course delivery, does that mean teaching?

33
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:05,020
Yeah, I suppose so. Well

34
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:09,095
what I thought was really good on this course was the standard of teaching.

35
00:02:09,095 --> 00:02:12,860
Actually. I mean some of the teachers were better than others

36
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,642
but the standard generally was fine.

37
00:02:14,642 --> 00:02:17,600
Much better than other courses I've been on.

38
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:22,710
Yeah, I agree. Let's put that then. What about suggestions for improvement?

39
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:26,660
I... I didn't think it was all that wonderful

40
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:31,400
when we had great long group discussion sessions that went on for hours

41
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:35,680
and hours. I don't mean we shouldn't have group discussions

42
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:38,510
just that they shouldn't go on too long.

43
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:41,920
Now, on to materials and equipment.

44
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:45,560
Oh, now what was good about some sessions was the handouts.

45
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:48,780
Yes, I thought all the handouts were good actually

46
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,760
and some were great, with website addresses and everything.

47
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,000
One problem though with materials was the key texts.

48
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,837
Yes! There just weren't enough copies on reserve in the library.

49
00:02:59,837 --> 00:03:03,720
And if you can't get the key texts before the session

50
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:06,464
how are you supposed to do the reading?

51
00:03:06,464 --> 00:03:10,650
And not enough computers. You have to wait ages to get one.

52
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:14,820
OK, testing and evaluation-well, I don't know

53
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:17,400
it's hard to say until we've got our written assignments back.

54
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:21,313
Don't talk about it, I only got mine in yesterday,

55
00:03:21,353 --> 00:03:26,470
it was a real struggle. I hate to think what mark I'll get

56
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:30,358
Yes, but at least we've done the oral presentation. I thought that was good,

57
00:03:30,358 --> 00:03:32,750
the way I got my feedback really quickly.

58
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:37,944
Yes, it was. And I liked the way we knew what we'd be evaluated on,

59
00:03:37,944 --> 00:03:43,830
we knew the criteria, so we knew we had to think about clarity, organisation, and so on.

60
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:47,082
Yeah, but I'm not so sure about the written work.

61
00:03:47,082 --> 00:03:51,310
One thing I think is that there's just too much, it's really stressful.

62
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:57,400
Yes, I'd agree and I don't see why they can't let us know the criteria they use for marking.

63
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,670
The written assignments? But he told us.

64
00:03:59,670 --> 00:04:05,060
No, for the final exams. What are they looking for. What are the criteria

65
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,220
What makes a pass or a fail?

66
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:10,480
Yeah, I never thought of that. It'd be really useful.

67
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,400
OK, any other comments?

68
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:16,260
I thought student support was excellent.

69
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:22,460
Yeah, me too. OK, excellent. Other comments?

70
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:24,840
No, I can't think of anything else.

71
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:29,400
Nor me. OK, so that's done. Thanks, Ben.

72
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,000
No, thank you.
